WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I want to talk about
gun control and this moment

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:05.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's happening right now
after the tragedy at Parkland.

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:09.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you feel that there
is actual pressure

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:12.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
on your colleagues
in the Senate?

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:15.248
Are these children actually
putting enough pressure on them

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:16.649 line:92%
that change might happen here?

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:18.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I really do.
I was at that March,

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:20.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it is something
I'm never gonna forget.

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:22.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
For years,
as a former prosecutor,

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:24.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
we've worked with
law enforcement to try to get

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:28.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
some sensible gun legislation
in, for safety's sake.

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:30.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have then moved on.
That didn't work.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:32.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then,
the moms, after Sandy Hook,

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:34.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
I remember them
sitting in my office,

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.670
telling the stories
of sitting in that fire station,

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:40.774 size:88% position:44%
waiting as, one by one,
these kids would come in

00:00:40.774 --> 00:00:42.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be reunited
with their parents,

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:44.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
and after a while,
those moms knew

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.846
they were never gonna see
their little kid again.

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:48.248 line:92%
Hearing that story and thinking

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:50.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
they couldn't get
the legislation passed

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:52.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
with those stories,
and then finally,

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:55.121 size:81% position:41%
Congress keeps trying,
we put forward bills

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:59.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
like I have on domestic abuse,
bills on background checks,

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:02.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, finally,
we are all gonna be bested

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:03.263 line:92%
by a bunch of 16-year-olds.

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:05.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I am
really psyched about that.

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:08.635
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I'm glad you're psyched.

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:12.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I just -- I think that,
when a kid looks

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:13.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
at their parent
or their grandparent,

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:16.776
even in my state, where we have
a proud hunting tradition,

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:18.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they say,
"Look, hunting's fine,

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:22.515
but we don't understand why we
can't go to school and be safe."

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:24.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's real hard
to say no to those kids.

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:28.154
-So I want to talk -- because
you do come from a rural state

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:31.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
that has a very
robust hunting community

00:01:31.658 --> 00:01:36.563
and NRA members -- NRA members
who want more gun legislation.

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:39.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I always felt this moment
means, "Look, anyone --"

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:42.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think it's very fair to have
issue with NRA leadership.

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:44.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think that
there are NRA members

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:47.173 size:88% position:44%
who have that membership
for a different reason.

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:50.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
They believe
in having a hunting rifle

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:54.581 size:88% position:44%
or maybe even, you know,
a handgun in the home.

00:01:54.581 --> 00:01:58.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are there NRA members
that are on --

00:01:58.485 --> 00:02:00.954 size:78% position:39%
or hold your position
on assault weapons

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:04.390
and on background checks,
and are they gonna be vocal

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:05.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
in this movement
that's happening?

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:09.195
-I mean, the polls show that
the majority of gun owners

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:10.597 line:92%
want to see background checks.

00:02:10.597 --> 00:02:13.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have the vast majority
of Americans

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:15.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
that want to see
better background checks.

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:16.603 size:78% position:39%
You had the President
of the United States

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:18.605
at a meeting, where I sat
right across from him,

00:02:18.605 --> 00:02:19.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
that said he wanted
to see background checks.

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:22.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But did you think that
he meant it when he said it?

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:24.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, well...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:25.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm gonna get to that
in a minute.

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:27.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, good, yeah.
-Okay, so --

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:28.648 line:92%
So there are just so many people

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:31.217
that want to see
these sensible gun legislation,

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:32.519 line:92%
so I think it's got to happen.

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:34.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
But right now,
the NRA does have a sway

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:35.622 line:92%
over so many of my colleagues.

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:41.094 size:81% position:41%
It's about, of course,
the very false premise

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:42.762 size:84% position:42%
that's put out there
that they're gonna just

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:43.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
take their guns away,
when, in fact,

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:46.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
there's no legislation
that's proposed to do that.

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:50.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, secondly, the money,
and it's out there.

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:52.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's money,
dark money from the outside.

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:55.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, you were at that meeting
with the President.

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:56.543
-Yes.
-That was very surreal to watch.

00:02:56.543 --> 00:03:00.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because you don't usually see
cameras in those meetings

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:02.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you have members
of both parties

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:04.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
talking to the President
very openly

00:03:04.784 --> 00:03:06.019 line:92%
about different gun legislation.

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:08.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
He seemed very agreeable
to a lot

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:13.059 size:84% position:42%
that was coming from
the left of that issue.

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:14.761 line:92%
He seemed pro-background checks.

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:18.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
He even criticized
his colleagues

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:20.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
and said that
they were afraid of the NRA

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:22.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that they didn't
have to be afraid of the NRA

00:03:22.569 --> 00:03:25.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
because he wasn't
beholden to the NRA.

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:26.639 line:92%
That went away pretty quickly.

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:29.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
In that room, do you --
did you --

00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:30.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
did your colleagues know
that this was show

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:33.112
and that nothing was being said
would have any permanence?

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:36.216
-Well, you want to hope so much
for those kids

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:37.317 line:92%
and those moms I just described,

00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:39.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
so you want to believe,
and he was actually listening.

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:42.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
He wasn't tweeting
anytime during the meeting.

00:03:42.789 --> 00:03:43.323 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:46.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he looked right across,
and he said not one,

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:48.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
not three times,
but nine times, I counted,

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:51.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
that he wanted to see
universal background checks.

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:55.068
And he said he endorsed my bill
when I explained to him

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:58.838
that 6,000 women have been
killed by their partners

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:01.140 line:92%
with guns in an 11-year period.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:03.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said
that's more than we've lost

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:05.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
of our brave soldiers
in Iraq and Afghanistan.

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:09.148
And he said,
"Include Amy's piece in there."

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:10.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so the problem was,
we then went on,

00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:14.654
and he got behind two good bills
but very narrow things

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:17.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
to improve background checks
and for safe schools.

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:19.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
He did that,
and that's all they've done.

00:04:19.392 --> 00:04:22.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, he met with the NRA
the next night,

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:23.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then we never heard
anything again

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:24.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
about universal
background checks

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:28.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
or anything again about
the domestic-violence bill.

00:04:28.468 --> 00:04:29.569 line:92%
And so we are not gonna give up,

00:04:29.569 --> 00:04:32.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
and certainly those kids
aren't gonna let us give up.

00:04:32.772 --> 00:04:34.340 line:92%
-I am happy to hear that.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:38.044 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:38.044 --> 00:04:41.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've been, obviously,
doing this for a while now.

00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:44.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've had some success.
What was your first day like?

00:04:44.284 --> 00:04:46.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
What was your first day
as a senator like?

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:48.721 size:75% position:38%
-Well, my first day,
I will not forget.

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:49.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
I came from
a little different background

00:04:49.989 --> 00:04:55.395
than some of the other Senators
and drove up there in my Saturn.

00:04:55.395 --> 00:04:57.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we have
our first fancy lunch.

00:04:57.697 --> 00:04:59.032 size:84% position:42% line:92%
No longer made, I know.

00:04:59.032 --> 00:05:00.667 line:92%
We have our first fancy lunch.

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:02.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there we are
in the LBJ room --

00:05:02.402 --> 00:05:05.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
this major portrait
of Lyndon Johnson above us.

00:05:05.171 --> 00:05:08.708
And I go over and I grab
a salad and a cup of soup,

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:09.642 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I bring it back.

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:11.511 line:92%
Fancy place, ready to dive in.

00:05:11.511 --> 00:05:13.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
And all of a sudden,
Patty Murray,

00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:15.882
the only woman at the table
besides myself, jumps up,

00:05:15.882 --> 00:05:19.052
runs around, grabs my arm,
and says, "Amy, you just took

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:21.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
the entire bowl
of thousand-island dressing,

00:05:21.087 --> 00:05:23.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you're about to eat it."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.323 --> 00:05:25.825
And I said,
"That's what we do in Minnesota.

00:05:25.825 --> 00:05:28.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
We eat the thousand-island
dressing."

00:05:28.227 --> 00:05:29.762 line:92%
But what I learned that day is,

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:32.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I still
try to keep it as my mantra,

00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:34.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Never forget
where you came from,

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
no matter what happens
in that place."

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:38.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
And if you want
to go into politics,

00:05:38.404 --> 00:05:41.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
if we want more women
and younger people to do,

00:05:41.941 --> 00:05:43.343 line:92%
you're gonna confront obstacles,

00:05:43.343 --> 00:05:45.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're gonna have
embarrassing moments,

00:05:45.345 --> 00:05:46.779 size:84% position:42% line:92%
but just don't give up.

00:05:46.779 --> 00:05:48.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, thank you so much
for being here.

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:50.083 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Really appreciate it.

00:05:50.083 --> 00:05:52.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
Senator Amy Klobuchar,
everybody.

